# Testing

## Where tests go

- Unit: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { use super::*; ... }` at the bottom of the file under test (private items reachable).
- Integration: `crates/<crate>/tests/<scenario>.rs`, one scenario per file, public API only (`round_trip.rs`).
- CLI end-to-end: `crates/shellzip-cli/tests/cli.rs` with `assert_cmd` + `predicates`; assert exit code and stdout/stderr text.
- Fixtures: build them in `tempfile::tempdir()` inside the test. Commit binaries under `fixtures/` only when produced by an external tool, with SHA-256 in `fixtures/SHA256SUMS` checked by the test.

## Writing tests

- Name = behaviour, snake_case, no `test_` prefix: `rejects_escape_and_reserved`, `add_to_an_existing_zip_keeps_previous_files`.
- One behaviour per test. A round-trip is add → list → test → extract → byte compare.
- `unwrap` / `expect` are fine in tests.
- Table-driven for many inputs: loop over a slice of cases and put the case in the assertion message.
- Platform-specific behaviour: `#[cfg(unix)]` / `#[cfg(windows)]` on the test. `#[ignore]` is not a fix.
- New behaviour ships with a test; a bug fix ships with the test that failed before the fix.

```rust
#[test]
fn detects_magic_bytes() {
    let cases: &[(&[u8], Format)] = &[
        (b"PK\x03\x04", Format::Zip),
        (b"\x1f\x8b", Format::Gz),
    ];
    for (bytes, want) in cases {
        assert_eq!(detect_bytes(bytes), Some(*want), "input {bytes:?}");
    }
}
```

## Fakes over mocks

- `ProgressSink` → `NopProgress` or a counting fake; `Read` / `Write` → `std::io::Cursor<Vec<u8>>`; prompts → a closure `ConflictDecider`.
- If a dependency has no trait boundary, add one at the seam before testing around it. Never use global state to inject behaviour.
- `mockall` only when a hand-written fake would be unwieldy.

## Edge cases archive code must cover

Empty file, empty dir, unicode names, zip-slip names (`../evil`, `/etc/passwd`, `C:\evil`, `dir/CON.txt`), symlink escaping dest, overwrite modes, wrong password → exit 11, interruption leaves no partial file.

Run `cargo test --workspace` before finishing; `cargo test -p <crate> <name>` while iterating. Patterns for `proptest` and `insta` are in the `rust-testing` skill.
